Compile the Suunto JSON importer without the FIT and multi-file paths.

`import-suunto-json.cpp` reads the JSON the Suunto app exports (Nautic, Ocean,
EON Core/Steel, D5). Two parts of it reach outside what this build compiles:

 - patch_from_fit() parses the .fit file the app writes next to the .json
   through libdc_buffer_parser(), i.e. the libdivecomputer download path
   (core/libdivecomputer.cpp), which is Qt-coupled and out of scope here. It
   only contributes the gas mix and the gradient factors; the profile itself
   comes from the JSON either way. Gutted, with a note when a FIT buffer is
   passed anyway.
 - suunto_json_fit_pair_import() pairs .json/.fit files chosen in a desktop file
   dialog. It needs QFile/QFileInfo and file.cpp's readfile(). The mobile app
   imports one file at a time, so it is dropped; the declaration in file.h stays
   and simply has no definition in this build.

Everything that maps JSON to dives - the header, the samples, the events, the
gases - is compiled unchanged. The Qt JSON classes it uses are provided by
cpp/shim/include/QJson* over nlohmann::json, so no other change is needed.

